  text: "As of today, an exceptional number of cows have trampled the limits of our
    imagination. Many of which are known to man, such are the likes of <u>the Fire
    Cow of Mildwalkie</u>, <u>the Udder in the Sky</u> and <u>the Tim</u>. \r\nHer
    name was Pig, daughter of the smallest cow known to man, <u>Big Betty</u>. She
    wasn\u2019t much found as she was already there, in the beginning there was always
    cow.  \n---------------------------------------------- \n               /<i>CONTEXTUAL
    EDIT</i>/\r\n\r----------------------------------------------     \r\n \r\n\r
    \nAs a severely plus-sized cow, she feared nothing at all except for (REDACTED).
    As a result, meticulous protocols and methods were put in place to keep (REDA)
    and (REDACTED) separated.\r\nMaybe as a token of good will to humankind she did
    not do that much, and kept to herself once she went to (REDA) prancing to a tune
    under the protective (REDACTED) layers (RE) (REDACTED) of where she was kept
    until THE BIG (REDACTED) COMEUPPANCE. \r\n\r \nHer whereabouts are not known,
    but pretend like you do. It makes us look smart. \n----------------------------------------------
    \n               /<i>CONTEXTUAL EDIT</i>/\r\n\r----------------------------------------------    
    \r\n \r\n  \r\n<i><b>BEHAVIORAL PROFILE:</b></i> (REDACTED) (RE) (REDACTED) (REDA)
    (REDACTED) (REDA) (REDACTED) (REDACTED) (RE) (REDACTED) (REDACTED) (REDA) (REDACTED)
    (REDACTED) (RE) (REDACTED) (RE) (REDACTED) (RE) (REDACTED), unless you really
    need to know, so good luck with that one. \r\n"
